            B.q("ai-m2-2", "ai-acr", "Every build must make the image, run the unit tests inside it, and push it only if the tests pass, all inside Azure. Which two pieces do you need? Select two.", listOf("A YAML task file (for example acr-task.yaml) with a build step, a cmd step that runs the tests, and a push step", "The registry admin user switched on so the task can sign in", "A Premium tier registry, because tasks need it", "az acr run -f acr-task.yaml, or a saved task made with az acr task create --file acr-task.yaml, to run the steps in ACR"), setOf(0, 3), "A multi-step ACR task is described in a YAML file: build makes the image, cmd runs a container from it (here the tests), and push uploads it. A failing step stops the run, so a failed test means nothing is pushed. You run the file once with az acr run -f, or save it as a task with az acr task create --file so it can run on triggers.",
