            B.q("ai-m2-3", "ai-acr", "You removed the tag v1.4 from the reminders image, yet the registry's storage use did not go down. Why, and what actually frees the space?", listOf("Storage use is only recalculated once a month, so wait", "Untagging removes only the name. The manifest and its layers stay until you delete the manifest by its digest, for example az acr repository delete --name larkspur --image reminders@sha256:<digest>", "Tags are copied to every region, so geo-replication must be turned off first", "Run az acr login again so the portal shows fresh numbers"), setOf(1), "A tag is only a label that points at a manifest, the image's table of contents, which is identified by its digest (a sha256 hash of its content). az acr repository untag removes the label and leaves the image in place. Deleting the manifest by digest removes the image, and layers no other image shares are then freed.",
