            B.q("ai-m2-5", "ai-appservice-containers", "Which app setting keeps the /home folder on shared, persistent storage?", listOf("WEBSITES_ENABLE_APP_SERVICE_STORAGE=true", "WEBSITES_PORT=8080", "WEBSITE_RUN_FROM_PACKAGE=1", "SCM_DO_BUILD_DURING_DEPLOYMENT=true"), setOf(0), "On Linux custom containers, persistent storage is off by default, so anything written to /home is lost on restart. Setting WEBSITES_ENABLE_APP_SERVICE_STORAGE to true mounts App Service's shared storage at /home, so files survive restarts and every instance sees them. For large or busy file stores, Blob Storage or a mounted Azure Files share is usually the better home.",
