            B.q("ai-m2-16", "ai-cosmos-sdk", "Two devices can save the same plan at nearly the same moment, and the later save must not silently overwrite the earlier one. Which azure-cosmos call shape gives this optimistic concurrency (accept a write only if nobody changed the item since you read it)?", listOf("replace_item(item, body, etag=read_etag, match_condition=MatchConditions.IfNotModified), and handle 412 Precondition Failed by reloading", "upsert_item(body) with Strong consistency", "create_item(body), and on 409 Conflict delete and create again", "read_item twice and compare the two copies before calling replace_item"), setOf(0), "Every item has an _etag that changes on each write. Sending the etag you read with IfNotModified makes Cosmos DB reject the write with 412 if someone else wrote in between, so the app can reload and merge.",
                scenario = "Kestrel Travel's Android app lets a family edit one shared trip plan from several phones. Plans are stored in Cosmos DB for NoSQL.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
