            B.q("ai-m2-21", "ai-cosmos-vector", "The vector policy uses the euclidean distance function. The query returns scores 0.12, 0.48 and 1.30 for three lessons. Which lesson is most similar to the question?", listOf("The lesson scored 1.30", "The lesson scored 0.12", "The lesson scored 0.48", "They are equally similar; euclidean scores are not comparable"), setOf(1), "Euclidean distance runs from 0 upward, and a smaller distance means the vectors are closer, so 0.12 is the best match. With cosine and dot product it is the other way round: a higher score means more similar.",
