            B.q("ai-m2-56", "ai-opentelemetry", "Calls from the API to Azure Managed Redis through redis-py never appear as dependencies, although its HTTP calls do. What do you add?", listOf("A second call to configure_azure_monitor() after connecting to Redis", "OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=redis on the API container", "A traceparent field stored inside every cached value", "The opentelemetry-instrumentation-redis package, with RedisInstrumentor().instrument() at start-up"), setOf(3), "The Azure Monitor distro bundles a fixed set of instrumentations (web frameworks, requests, psycopg2, the Azure SDK and a few more). A library outside that set needs its own OpenTelemetry instrumentation package. Once it is instrumented, every Redis command becomes a dependency span inside the request's trace.",
                scenario = "Kitchenly's Python API caches recipe search results in Azure Managed Redis and sends telemetry to Application Insights.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
