                    2 to "Trace context travels with requests, not inside cached data, and a client span needs no stored context to be measured.",
                ),
            ),
            B.q("ai-m2-57", "ai-opentelemetry", "Container Apps health probes call /health every few seconds, and those requests make up most of the telemetry bill. How do you stop tracing them without losing other requests?", listOf("Lower the sampling rate to 1 percent for everything", "Set OTEL_PYTHON_EXCLUDED_URLS to health, so the web instrumentation creates no span for matching URLs", "Remove the health probes from the container app", "Delete the probe rows from the requests table every night"), setOf(1), "The OpenTelemetry Python web instrumentations read a list of excluded URLs (OTEL_PYTHON_EXCLUDED_URLS, or a framework-specific one such as OTEL_PYTHON_FASTAPI_EXCLUDED_URLS) and skip matching requests. The probes keep working; they simply stop producing telemetry.",
                scenario = "Parcelly's tracking API runs on Azure Container Apps with liveness and readiness probes, and sends traces to Application Insights.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "Sampling cuts every kind of trace alike, so real user requests are lost along with the probes.",
                    2 to "Probes let the platform restart unhealthy replicas. Removing them saves money by adding outage risk.",
                    3 to "You pay to ingest data when it arrives. Deleting it later does not undo that cost.",
                ),
            ),
            B.q("ai-m2-58", "ai-kql", "Sampling keeps only part of the telemetry. Which query estimates the real number of requests per hour?", listOf("AppRequests | summarize count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)", "AppRequests | summarize dcount(OperationId) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)", "AppRequests | take 1000 | count", "AppRequests | summarize sum(ItemCount) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)"), setOf(3), "Each record kept by sampling carries ItemCount, the number of original items it stands for (10 when one in ten is kept). Summing ItemCount estimates the true total; count() only counts the rows that were stored.",
                scenario = "Quizly keeps one trace in ten to control cost. The product manager asks how many quiz submissions the API handled each hour yesterday.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "count() counts the stored rows, so with sampling on it undercounts by roughly the sampling factor.",
                    1 to "Distinct operation ids still only covers the traces that sampling kept.",
                    2 to "take 1000 cuts the data to 1,000 rows before anything is counted.",
